{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAGegRGcVAALPuN7gHUF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've submitted index 0 (Sb fraction 0.085) as the best composition. It had the highest EQE I measured, 0.00293%. I used all 5 EQE measurements and 3 of the 5 XRD measurements.\n\nEvery result was very small. The illumination is 2.4 eV, which I expect is well below the band gap of Mg–Sb oxides, so these films barely respond. The chance of beating index 0 elsewhere on the line is modest.\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) | XRD |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0.085 | 0.00293 | not measured |\n| 4 | 0.126 | 0.00167 | Pt substrate peaks only, so the film is likely amorphous |\n| 29 | 0.807 | 0.00096 | Crystalline MgSb₂O₆ (trirutile) plus extra Sb |\n| 24 | 0.661 | 0.00011 | Mostly Pt, with a weak MgSb₂O₆ peak |\n| 14 | 0.350 | −0.00002 | not measured |\n\nEQE rose steadily toward the Mg-rich end, and index 0 is the lowest-Sb point on the line, so it's the best measured choice. The middle of the line was essentially zero. The Sb-rich end, including the crystalline MgSb₂O₆ film, came in lower than the Mg-rich end.\n\nI never measured indices 1–3, which sit between the two best points. Because the trend points to lower Sb, they're unlikely to beat index 0, but the budget ran out before I could confirm that."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":6895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"output_tokens":527,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"955e521f-ed8e-458d-a8c9-4068f322bd01","uuid":"2e5c6469-6e18-4527-9de7-1218f4226d1a","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:26:04.912Z","request_id":"req_011CfAGeg1DEzKdtMvE8cU72"}
